The United States House just passed my amendment to get us one step closer to making sure all of our military families have the child care that they need. I represent Military City, USA, and San Antonio, Texas, where you have so many military families. I've met with who face long wait lists or have to pay thousands of dollars to be able to get childcare while they're on base. while they're training. And that's just not right. And the Defense Department doesn't even really know how many of our service members are on these wait lists, how much they're paying, what it will take to make sure we solve this problem. My amendment is the critical first step to getting the problem solved by requiring a study to make sure we get the information that we need to solve the child care crisis for our service members, who dedicate so much to our country, while we also work to solve the child care crisis for every single working family in America.
